  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, $\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y+1}{x-1}$<br />$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{d y}{y+1}=\\frac{d x}{x-1}$<br />After integrating on both sides, we have<br />$\\log (y+1)=\\log (x-1)-\\log C$<br />$C(y+1)=(x-1)$<br />$C=\\frac{x-1}{y+1}$<br />If $x=1$, then $y=2$, so $C=0$ <br />Therefore, $x-1=0$ <br />Hence, there is only one solution.",
    "image": null
  },
